		"instructions":"
<h2>Play</h2>
<p>Each move, you move a piece one space along a line. Capturing is compulsory, and results under the following circumstances:</p>
<ul>
<li><em>Approach</em> After the move, there are one or more enemy pieces directly in front of the moving piece; they are captured.</li>
<li><em>Withdrawal</em> Before the move, there were one or more enemy pieces directly behind the moving piece; they are captured.</li>
</ul>
<p>If both of the above apply, choose one.</p>
<p>After capturing, the same piece may move again; so long as each subsequent move results in a capture.
During the continuation moves, you may not move twice in the same direction, or revisit the same space.</p>

<h2>Goal</h2>
<p>Capture all your opponent's pieces to win.</p>

<h2>Variant</h2>
<p>There seems to be some debate as to whether continuation captures are optional or required.  Ai Ai allows you to choose.</p>


